WHAT THIS PHASE CORRECTED
1. Income ignored recorded payments. The report accrued from tenancy terms
   and presented the estimate as fact, while rental_payments - money
   actually received via the agent-email webhook - sat unused.
2. No apportionment at all. A part-owner saw 100% of the property's
   figures.
3. Loan interest, typically the largest rental deduction, was absent from
   the report entirely.
4. The interest estimate assumed a full year at the latest rate and
   ignored the offset account. On the user's own loan that overstated by
   32%.

RULES ENCODED (with tests)
- Ownership scales income AND deductions; availability and private use
  scale DEDUCTIONS ONLY. Reducing income by availability would understate
  assessable rent. Asserted from both directions.
- Only CONFIRMED loan statements are claimable. Verified live: two
  statements, one confirmed and one pending -> claimable 21,450 not
  26,450; confirming the second at an EDITED amount used the edit.
- Divergence thresholds 5% AND $500 together, so a missing month (~8%)
  flags while rent straddling 30 June (~2%) does not.
- null vs 0 for income: no records means unknown, not "no rent received".

